! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262's INTERRUPT ENTRY and constant pool
! -- PDF p.109 whole, octal 024172.00-024331.00, 54 printed rows.
! Transcribed VERBATIM at the listing's own addresses and checked
! bit-exactly by verify_ax5b_162_int_entry_listing.py.
!
! THE ROW THE PAGE EXISTS FOR:
!
!     024320.00  I62ITE  BD,$   "-ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE."  24320.04 00
!     024320.40          B,$                                   24320.50 00
!
! One FULL WORD holding two self-branches, and the two halves differ
! in exactly one thing: the .00 half is BRANCH DISABLED and the .40
! half is BRANCH.  Reference Manual printed p.40 (PDF p.43): "Branch
! Disabled (BD).  This operation DISABLES the interruption mechanism,
! and then performs the same operation as BRANCH"; BRANCH alone leaves
! the state untouched.  So the landing half CHOOSES whether the
! interrupt routine runs disabled or stays enabled, and routine 1262
! picks one per test by storing a different constant into the table:
!
!     024172.00  I62K1  BD,I62ITE     24320.04 00   -> lands at .00
!     024177.00  I62K6  B,I62ITE+.32  24320.50 00   -> lands at .40
!
! Each is a full word with the same half-word instruction in BOTH
! halves, which is what lets one "SX,$X2,I62INT%$X1@" write it into a
! 64-word table entry.  p.93 shows the fill loop for both, at 023474.40
! ("-DO BE AND BD.", I62K6) and 023522.00 ("-DO BB, SETUP BD INT TBL.",
! I62K1).
!
! WHICH HALF DOES A TEST AIM AT?  Read the octal pair's TOP BIT, which
! is bit 18, the half-word select: I62K1's "04" = 000100 has bit 18 =
! 0, so 024320.00, the BD half; I62K6's "50" = 101000 has bit 18 = 1,
! so 024320.40, the B half.  The rule the pages show is TRANSPARENCY,
! not "enabled": the B half is chosen wherever the landing must not
! change the enable state, because the block is about to MEASURE it --
! p.93's I6225 probes "am I still disabled?" and I6229/I6232 probes
! "am I still enabled?", and both write "SVA,$X1,I62ITE+.32".  The BD
! half is used where disabling on landing costs nothing, as in TEST 3A
! and TEST 3B (pp.107-108), whose landing is the end of the test; both
! write "SVA,$X1,I62ITE".
!
! ONE CONJECTURE, FLAGGED.  That the table still holds I62K1 when TEST
! 3B runs is not read: pp.94-107 were not swept.  p.93's I6233 block
! ("-DO BB, SETUP BD INT TBL.") is the last table fill seen, and it
! loads I62K1.  The internal argument is strong -- if the table still
! held I62K6 the interrupt would land at I62ITE+.32, which 3A/3B never
! SVA, so the landing would be the untouched "B,$" self-loop and
! neither block could pass -- but it is an argument, not a page.
!
! AND SVA REWRITES ONLY THE ADDRESS FIELD.  Reference Manual printed
! p.29 (PDF p.32), "Store Value in Address (SVA)": "The first 18, 19,
! or 24 bits of the value field of the index word specified by J
! replace THE ADDRESS FIELD of the instruction specified by the
! effective address", the width being "determined from the instruction
! operation code".  A half-word branch's address field is bits 0-18 --
! 19 bits, bit 18 included -- so an SVA into I62ITE plants a full
! half-word-resolved target and leaves "BD" standing.  The op is never
! rewritten; only the address is.
!
! THE TABLE ITSELF.  "I62INT DR%BU,64,8@,64 -INTRPT TABLE." at
! 024220.00 prints "100.00" in the machine-code column -- that is the
! RESERVE SIZE, 0o100 = 64 words, not a machine word, so NO WORD IS
! FABRICATED for it here: the transcription SLCs across the reserve and
! takes the label by SYN.  The arithmetic checks: 024220 + 0o100 =
! 024320, exactly where the page prints I62ITE.  Ref. Manual printed
! p.48 (PDF p.51) describes the table as "48 successive full-word
! locations" (indicators 48-63 are permanently masked off); the deck
! reserves 64 and points $IA at it with I62XW1, "XW,0,64,I62INT" at
! 024326.00, whose refill-address field holds 024220.
!
! WHAT ELSE IS ON THE PAGE.  I62B1-I62B16 (024200.00-024217.00) are
! the SUBJECT-INSTRUCTION pairs the EX/EXIC tests execute -- each a
! branch that should be suppressed by EXE plus the branch that is
! taken when it is not (Ref. Manual printed p.49: "The execution
! exception indicator (EXE) is turned on by any branch operation of a
! subject instruction in which the condition for a successful branch is
! met ... The suppressed actions include the disabling in BRANCH
! DISABLED, the enabling in BRANCH ENABLED").  I62B3 is the "BE" pair
! and I62B4 the "BD" pair that p.93's I6225/I6229 blocks execute.
! I62EX-I62EXM (024322.00-024331.00) are the subject instructions
! themselves, under the comment "-KEEP / -IN / -ORDER", with I62PSI
! the pseudo-IC word and I62SUB the subject slot.
!
! A HOLE AT 024325.40, and it is the listing's, not this file's.
! I62BR2 "$BD,0" is a half-word at 024325.00 and I62XW1 is an XW,
! which must start on a word boundary, so the page jumps straight to
! 024326.00.  This assembler aligns full-word items by itself -- the
! half-word is left untouched rather than filled -- so no SLC is
! needed and no row is asserted there.
!
! THE FOUR CNOPs ARE A FREE SELF-CHECK on that same alignment rule.
! Two of them print a NOP word (024207.40 and 024217.40, both at an
! ODD half-word) and two print nothing at all (the one above I62K1 and
! the one above I62EX, both already word-aligned).  All four are kept
! verbatim, and the assembler reproduces the pattern.  Measured, not
! assumed: removing CNOP's alignment moves seven labels and fifteen
! rows -- from the first ODD-half-word CNOP to the end of the I62B run
! and nowhere else, because the SLC across the table re-anchors what
! follows.  See the verify script's injection table.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: three, and a fourth retired.  (1) RETIRED: this item
! used to read "numeric labels prefixed L", the prefix being needed
! because this assembler reads a leading digit as an address.  The
! leading glyph was measured at 600 dpi and it is the LETTER I, so
! the page's own spellings -- I6221..I6299, I62B1..I62B16, I62BR1/2,
! I62EX*, I62INT, I62ITE, I62K1..I62K6, I62PSI, I62SUB, I62XW1 and
! I00O -- are legal STRAP-1 symbols unaided and are written as printed
! (docs/listing_typography.md).  (2) "%8@n"
! -> "(8)n" and "%BU@"/"%U@" -> "(BU)"/"(U)", this repo's spellings.
! (3) "I62INT%$X1@" does not appear here (it is on p.93).  (4) THE
! "$BD,0" ROWS: I62BR1 at 024323.40 and I62BR2 at 024325.00 are
! printed "$BD,0" and written "BD,0" here.  The 32 bits are identical
! -- both are the printed "0.04 00", measured -- but what STRAP's "$"
! prefix on an operation MEANS is not established by any page read for
! this work; it occurs only on data-in-the-instruction-stream rows
! (these two, and I60SX1 at 023041.00).  Left as an open question.
!
! ENCODING ONLY.  Nothing here is executed in place: the page is a
! constant pool plus the one landing word.
!
! EXTERNALS are SYN'd at the addresses these same rows print for them,
! bit 18 decoded out of the printed octal pair in each case.  EVERY
! SYN IS AN INPUT TO THE CHECK, NOT A WITNESS -- it makes the address
! field come out right by construction, so a row naming one proves
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.

I6221  SYN, (8)23464.0            ! 24 branch targets in 1262's body,
I6224  SYN, (8)23473.40           ! each from this page's own printed
I6225  SYN, (8)23474.40           ! address, bit 18 = top bit of the
I6226  SYN, (8)23504.0            ! octal pair.  p.93 confirms I6225,
I6227  SYN, (8)23505.0            ! I6226, I6227, I6231 and I6232 in
I6231  SYN, (8)23516.40           ! its own label column.
I6232  SYN, (8)23517.40
I6234  SYN, (8)23535.0
I6235  SYN, (8)23536.40
I6238  SYN, (8)23543.0
I6239  SYN, (8)23544.40
I6246  SYN, (8)23571.0
I6274  SYN, (8)24025.0
I6277  SYN, (8)24034.0
I6278  SYN, (8)24035.0
I6279  SYN, (8)24045.40
I6280  SYN, (8)24046.40
I6284  SYN, (8)24060.40
I6285  SYN, (8)24061.40
I6287  SYN, (8)24072.40
I6288  SYN, (8)24074.0
I6291  SYN, (8)24101.40
I6292  SYN, (8)24103.0
I6299  SYN, (8)24130.40
I00O   SYN, (8)24503.0            ! the deck's own label "I00O"
I62INT SYN, (8)24220.0            ! the reserve: see the header
        SLC, (8)24172.0
!
! ---- the constants routine 1262 stores into the interrupt table ----
        CNOP                       ! -CONSTANTS FOR 1262.  (aligned: no word)
I62K1  BD,  I62ITE               ! -> the DISABLED landing half
        BD,  I62ITE
I62K2  EX,  I62EXT
        EX,  I62EXT
I62K3  EX,  $X3
        EX,  $X3
I62K4  EX,  $L
        EX,  $L
I62K5  EXIC, $+.32
        EXIC, $+.32
I62K6  B,   I62ITE+.32           ! -> the ENABLED landing half
        B,   I62ITE+.32
!
! ---- the subject-instruction branch pairs --------------------------
I62B1  BXVZ, $+.32
        BD,  I6221
I62B2  BXVZ, I6224
        B,   I6225
I62B3  BE,  I6226                ! the "BE" pair, executed at 023502.00
        B,   I6227
I62B4  BD,  I6231                ! the "BD" pair, executed at 023514.40
        B,   I6232
I62B5  BB,  $X0, I6234
        B,   I6235
I62B6  BB,  $X0+.01, I6238
        B,   I6239
I62B7  BD,  I6246
        CNOP                       ! odd half-word: prints 0.30 00
I62B10 BXVZ, $+.32
        BD,  I6274
I62B11 BXVZ, I6277
        B,   I6278
I62B12 BE,  I6279
        B,   I6280
I62B13 BD,  I6284
        B,   I6285
I62B14 BB,  $X0, I6287
        B,   I6288
I62B15 BB,  $X0+.01, I6291
        B,   I6292
I62B16 BD,  I6299
        CNOP                       ! odd half-word: prints 0.30 00
!
! ---- I62INT, "DR%BU,64,8@,64  -INTRPT TABLE.", 024220.00 -----------
!      64 words reserved, printed "100.00" = the SIZE.  No machine
!      word exists to transcribe; SLC across it.  024220 + 0o100 =
!      024320, which is the next printed address.
        SLC, (8)24320.0
!
! ---- the landing word ----------------------------------------------
I62ITE BD,  $                     ! -ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE.
        B,   $
I62EXT XW,  0, 0, 0
!
! ---- the subject instructions, "-KEEP / -IN / -ORDER" --------------
        CNOP                       ! aligned after the XW: no word
I62EX  LX,  $X1, I00O            ! -IN
        NOP                        ! -ORDER
I62PSI LX,  $X0, 0                ! -PSEUDO IC.
I62BR1 BD,  0                     ! listing: "$BD,0"
I62SUB XW,  0, 0, 0               ! -SUBJ INST.
I62BR2 BD,  0                     ! listing: "$BD,0"; 024325.40 is skipped
I62XW1 XW,  0, 64, I62INT        ! the $IA setting: 64 words at I62INT
I62EXV L(BU), I00O               ! -VFL FULL WD.
I62EXF L(U), I00O                ! -FLT PT.
        L(U), I00O
I62EXM Z,   $X1                   ! -MISC.
        END, I62ITE
